"kind": "witness",
"submitted_by": "arhancanli",
"date": "2026-11-08",
"notes": "A weak Schur partition of [1, 2154] into 7 sets: Rowley's first construction (rowley-2020, Theorem 1: WS(k+1) >= 4 S(k) + 2) applied to Adam McKenna's partition of [1, 538] into 6 sum-free sets (\"The sixth Schur number is at least 538\", Zenodo, 4 Nov 2026, doi:10.5281/zenodo.23937655, file schur6-538.word, colours renumbered in the order of their least elements). T_i = {4i - 1, 4i, 4i + 1} takes the colour of i for i in [1, 538], and {1, 2, 6, 10, ..., 2154} is the seventh colour. This improves the published WS(7) >= 2146 (Rowley, from S(6) >= 536). Built by our own script and checked by three programs of our own (a C bitset scan over each colour class, a NumPy FFT convolution and an exact number-theoretic transform modulo 2013265921), written by an AI agent (Claude, Anthropic) for Quantavane; each rejects a copy with one number recoloured.",
"path": "certificates/weak-schur/weak-schur-7-lower-2154.yml",
"status": "verified",
"role": "discovery"
}
